All 46 tests pass.

The fix replaces `new Date(y, m, d).getTime()` (local midnight, whose UTC offset shifts across DST) with `Date.UTC(y, m, d)` for both the due date and today. `Date.UTC` always returns an offset-free UTC midnight, so the millisecond difference is always an exact multiple of 86 400 000. `Math.round` is used instead of `Math.floor` as a belt-and-suspenders guard against any sub-millisecond floating-point noise, though with integer UTC values it makes no practical difference.[INFO] [KRS] <-- GenerateAssistantResponseCommand done totalEvents=63

